WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.357
Before you choose your BOOST pathway, let

2
00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:04.412
me quickly explain how this works.

3
00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:06.954
BOOST has two pathways, but they both

4
00:00:06.954 --> 00:00:09.567
lead toward the same goal —employment.

5
00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:12.585
The Rapid Employment Pathway is designed for people who

6
00:00:12.585 --> 00:00:15.279
are ready to move toward work more quickly.

7
00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:18.112
It focuses on practical employment readiness,

8
00:00:18.112 --> 00:00:22.152
financial stability, transferable skills, AI tools,

9
00:00:22.152 --> 00:00:24.160
and job- search support.

10
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.703
The Career Exploration and Development Pathway

11
00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:28.781
gives you more opportunity to explore

12
00:00:28.781 --> 00:00:30.848
and validate a career direction.

13
00:00:30.848 --> 00:00:34.076
You’ll look more closely at jobs, wages, career

14
00:00:34.076 --> 00:00:38.650
fit, transferable skills, industry options, and whether additional

15
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.960
development or training is really needed.

16
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.050
One pathway isn’t better than the other.

17
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.419
They simply respond to different needs.

18
00:00:45.419 --> 00:00:46.893
And this decision isn’t based on

19
00:00:46.893 --> 00:00:49.482
a single test or one answer.

20
00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:52.129
Through your conversations with your Career Coach, the

21
00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:53.778
evidence may show that it makes sense to

22
00:00:53.778 --> 00:00:56.390
prioritize one pathway over the other.

23
00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.385
That decision is made individually, based on the

24
00:00:59.385 --> 00:01:02.323
skills and experience you already have, the career

25
00:01:02.323 --> 00:01:05.051
direction you’re considering, and how those things align

26
00:01:05.051 --> 00:01:07.675
with opportunities in the current labor market.

27
00:01:07.675 --> 00:01:10.531
Your pathway can also change as you learn more.

28
00:01:10.531 --> 00:01:13.387
New information, new opportunities, or what

29
00:01:13.387 --> 00:01:15.360
you discover about yourself may point

30
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.299
toward a different next step.

31
00:01:17.299 --> 00:01:19.691
You don’t have to figure that out alone.

32
00:01:19.691 --> 00:01:21.700
Your Career Coach will help you review the

33
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.335
evidence and determine which pathway gives you the

34
00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:27.342
strongest and most efficient route forward.

35
00:01:27.342 --> 00:01:30.685
Whichever path you take, the goal remains the same:

36
00:01:30.685 --> 00:01:31.614
help you move toward

37
00:01:31.614 --> 00:01:33.959
meaningful, sustainable employment.

38
00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:36.920
When you’re ready, let’s choose your BOOST pathway.
